Register the Rust toolchains by recursive pattern, not `//:all`.

aspect_rules_lint_rust declares `rules_rs` 0.0.83 and registers
`@default_rust_toolchains//:all`. This repository resolves rules_rs 0.0.106,
which lays that repo out with the toolchains in subpackages -- `rustc/`,
`rustfmt/`, `rust-analyzer/` -- and no BUILD file at the root. `//:all` then
names a package that does not exist, and every toolchain resolution fails with
"BUILD file not found in directory ''".

`//...` matches the same toolchains under either layout.

The alternative was pinning rules_rs back to 0.0.83 across the whole build, to
suit a module used only for its clippy aspect.

--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -28,6 +28,6 @@
 use_repo(toolchains, "default_rust_toolchains")
 
 register_toolchains(
-    "@default_rust_toolchains//:all",
+    "@default_rust_toolchains//...",
     "@llvm//toolchain:all",
 )
